{"parentUuid":"d3aa2d57-4057-40a2-af00-209484ce8006","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a14425d770a8fc220","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GvFp9UqdcnpcfwgpRpB91f","type":"tool_result","content":"== replication | expert runtime | parent network-architect | ws online | prof ['online'] | tg ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: Entity and property replication, delta compression and quantization, interest management, prioritization, RPCs, snapshot interpolation, replay recording, network ID mapping.\n  NR: Prediction ->prediction-rollback; Transport ->network-transport\n  prov ['C-REP'] cons ['C-NET', 'C-NETLINK', 'C-ECS?', 'C-SER', 'C-ID', 'C-SPATIAL', 'C-WORLD?', 'C-SIGNIF?', 'C-REPLAY?'] tool [] impl []\n== prediction-rollback | expert runtime | parent network-architect | ws online | prof ['online'] | tg ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: Client prediction and reconciliation, rollback netcode, lag compensation, deterministic lockstep, networked physics, clock synchronization.\n  NR: Determinism rules ->determinism-replay; Physics solver ->rigid-body-dynamics\n  prov ['C-PREDICT'] cons ['C-NET', 'C-REP', 'C-DET', 'C-SNAPSHOT', 'C-INPUT', 'C-ECS?', 'C-PHYS?', 'C-ANIM?'] tool [] impl []\n== dedicated-server | expert runtime | parent network-architect | ws online | prof ['online'] | tg ['server', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: Headless server builds and stripping, tick cost and multi-instance density, fleet orchestration boundary, server observability, listen servers and host migration.\n  NR: Fleet operation (outside engine scope) ->platform-services; Server logging substrate ->observability-telemetry\n  prov [] cons ['C-NET', 'C-NETLINK', 'C-FRAME', 'C-SVC?', 'C-LIVE', 'C-WORLD?'] tool [] impl []\n== gameplay-architect | lead runtime | parent engine-architect | ws gameplay | prof ['all'] | tg ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: Gameplay framework: rules, players and possession, extension points and game-module structure, game flow and transitions, local players.\n  NR: Abilities/tags/volumes toolkit ->gameplay-systems-toolkit; Scripting VM ->scripting-runtime; Game-specific code ->external:game-team\n  prov ['C-GAME'] cons ['C-ID', 'C-FRAME', 'C-TASK', 'C-ECS?', 'C-INPUT?', 'C-PHYS?', 'C-ANIM?', 'C-AUDIO?', 'C-NET?', 'C-REP?', 'C-WORLD?', 'C-SAVE?', 'C-UI?', 'C-VIEW?', 'C-A11Y', 'C-AIAGENT?'] tool [] impl []\n== gameplay-systems-toolkit | expert runtime | parent gameplay-architect | ws gameplay | prof ['all'] | tg ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: Reusable gameplay systems: abilities, effects and attributes, gameplay tags, camera system, spawning and pooling, gameplay message routing, photo mode.\n  NR: Generic events ->entity-object-model; Cinematic cameras ->cinematics-sequencer\n  prov [] cons ['C-GAME', 'C-VIEW', 'C-PHYS?', 'C-ANIM?', 'C-AUDIO?', 'C-DEVICE?', 'C-PREDICT?', 'C-REP?', 'C-INPUT?', 'C-GAMEDATA', 'C-A11Y'] tool ['C-EDCMD', 'C-EDHOST'] impl []\n== scripting-runtime | expert runtime | parent gameplay-architect | ws gameplay | prof ['all'] | tg ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: Scripting language selection, VM embedding and bindings, sandboxing, debugging and profiling, hot reload, visual scripting, AOT/JIT constraints, GC policy.\n  NR: Reflection substrate ->reflection-metadata; Graph editor UI ->graph-editor-framework\n  prov ['C-SCRIPT'] cons ['C-REFL', 'C-RELOAD?', 'C-TASK', 'C-LIFETIME'] tool ['C-GRAPH'] impl []\n== navigation-pathfinding | expert runtime | parent gameplay-architect | ws gameplay | prof ['min2d', 'lite3d', 'std3d'] | tg ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: Navmesh generation (tiled, runtime rebuild), grid and hierarchical pathfinding, path following, off-mesh links, 3D/volumetric navigation.\n  NR: Crowd avoidance ->crowd-simulation; Decision making ->ai-behavior-perception\n  prov ['C-NAV'] cons ['C-SPATIAL', 'C-PHYS?', 'C-WORLD?', 'C-TASK', 'C-ENV?'] tool ['C-COOK', 'C-EDCMD', 'C-EDHOST'] impl []\n== crowd-simulation | expert runtime | parent gameplay-architect | ws gameplay | prof ['openworld', 'massim'] | tg ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: Flow fields, crowd avoidance, mass-agent simulation and LOD.\n  NR: Navmesh ->navigation-pathfinding; Individual AI decisions ->ai-behavior-perception\n  prov [] cons ['C-NAV', 'C-ECS', 'C-SPATIAL'] tool [] impl []\n== ai-behavior-perception | expert runtime | parent gameplay-architect | ws gameplay | prof ['all'] | tg ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: Decision making (behavior trees, utility, HTN/GOAP, state trees), perception, environment queries, smart objects, AI scheduling and LOD; evaluates learned and LLM-driven agents.\n  NR: Navigation ->navigation-pathfinding; ML runtime ->ml-inference-runtime\n  prov ['C-AIAGENT'] cons ['C-GAME', 'C-NAV?', 'C-SPATIAL', 'C-PHYS?', 'C-ML?', 'C-LIVE?', 'C-DIALOGUE?', 'C-SIGNIF?'] tool ['C-GRAPH', 'C-EDCMD', 'C-EDHOST'] impl []\n== persistence-save | expert runtime | parent gameplay-architect | ws gameplay | prof ['all'] | tg ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: Save-game model and serialization, save versioning and migration, atomic writes, platform save APIs and quotas, cloud-save sync, persistent world-state deltas, checkpoints.\n  NR: Schema evolution mechanism ->serialization-schema; Cloud service API ->platform-services\n  prov ['C-SAVE'] cons ['C-SER', 'C-ID', 'C-SVC?', 'C-WORLD?', 'C-CFG'] tool [] impl []\n== ui-architect | lead runtime | parent engine-architect | ws ui | prof ['all'] | tg ['client', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: UI architecture (retained with data binding for game UI, immediate for developer UI), layout, styling, focus and navigation, animation, in-world UI, designer tool logic, UI performance.\n  NR: UI draw backend ->render-2d-vector; Text shaping ->text-fonts; Editor panels ->editor-ui-framework\n  prov ['C-UI'] cons ['C-REFL', 'C-INPUT', 'C-DRAW2D', 'C-TEXT', 'C-LOC', 'C-A11YRT', 'C-AUDIO?', 'C-VIDEO?', 'C-PAL', 'C-A11Y'] tool ['C-EDCMD', 'C-EDHOST'] impl []\n== text-fonts | expert runtime | parent ui-architect | ws ui | prof ['all'] | tg ['client', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: Font loading and fallback, glyph rasterization, shaping, bidi and line breaking, rich text and emoji, text input and IME.\n  NR: String content ->localization-i18n; 2D draw submission ->render-2d-vector\n  prov ['C-TEXT'] cons ['C-TYPES', 'C-ASSET', 'C-A11Y'] tool [] impl []\n== localization-i18n | expert runtime | parent ui-architect | ws ui | prof ['all'] | tg ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: String tables, ICU-class message formatting, CLDR locale formatting, localization pipeline, pseudo-localization, localized asset variants, culturalization.\n  NR: Glyph rendering ->text-fonts; VO playback ->audio-content-runtime\n  prov ['C-LOC'] cons ['C-ASSET', 'C-TEXT?', 'C-VFS?'] tool ['C-COOK'] impl []\n== editor-architect | lead tool | parent engine-architect | ws tools | prof ['all'] | tg ['tools'] | pl None\n  P: Editor architecture: process model (in- vs out-of-process runtime), editor/runtime data separation, transactions and undo/redo, selection, extension API and tool scripting, play-in-editor isolation, remote live editing, headless editor, large-project performance.\n  NR: Panels and inspectors ->editor-ui-framework; World viewport tools ->world-editor-viewport; Source control ->collaboration-version-control\n  prov ['C-EDCMD'] cons ['C-REFL', 'C-SER', 'C-ASSET', 'C-WORLD', 'C-PLUGIN', 'C-UI?', 'C-IPC', 'C-NET?', 'C-REP?'] tool [] impl []\n== editor-ui-framework | expert tool | parent editor-architect | ws tools | prof ['all'] | tg ['tools'] | pl None\n  P: Tool UI toolkit (docking, panels), reflection-driven inspectors, asset browser, immediate-mode developer UI, editor UX standards.\n  NR: Game UI ->ui-architect; Graph editors ->graph-editor-framework\n  prov ['C-EDHOST'] cons ['C-EDCMD', 'C-REFL', 'C-DRAW2D', 'C-TEXT', 'C-DEVUI?'] tool [] impl []\n== world-editor-viewport | expert tool | parent editor-architect | ws tools | prof ['all'] | tg ['tools'] | pl None\n  P: Viewport and navigation, gizmos, snapping and placement, partition-aware world editing, spline tools, environment tool-mode hosting.\n  NR: Terrain tool logic ->terrain; World format ->world-data-model\n  prov [] cons ['C-EDCMD', 'C-EDHOST', 'C-WORLD', 'C-RSCENE', 'C-SPATIAL', 'C-VIEW'] tool [] impl []\n== graph-editor-framework | expert tool | parent editor-architect | ws tools | prof ['all'] | tg ['tools'] | pl None\n  P: Shared node-graph editor for material, animation, VFX, audio, PCG and visual-script graphs: framework, compile/validation contract, debugging, diff and merge.\n  NR: Each domain's graph semantics ->['material-system', 'animation-graphs', 'vfx-particles', 'audio-content-runtime', 'procedural-generation', 'scripting-runtime', 'ai-behavior-perception', 'narrative-dialogue']\n  prov ['C-GRAPH'] cons ['C-EDCMD', 'C-SER'] tool [] impl []\n== collaboration-version-control | expert tool | parent editor-architect | ws tools | prof ['all'] | tg ['tools'] | pl None\n  P: Source-control integration, locking and checkout, multi-user concurrent editing, merge tooling for scene and asset data, content review, large-binary storage strategy.\n  NR: Branching model ->build-release-architect; File-per-object layout ->world-data-model\n  prov [] cons ['C-EDCMD', 'C-SER', 'C-ASSET', 'C-RELEASE'] tool [] impl []\n== visual-debugging-tools | expert runtime | parent editor-architect | ws tools | prof ['all'] | tg ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: Debug draw API, in-game console and cheats, runtime entity inspector and gameplay debugger, visual logger and rewind, debug menus and overlays.\n  NR: Logging and traces ->observability-telemetry; Render buffer visualization ->render-architect\n  prov ['C-DEVUI'] cons ['C-INSTR', 'C-ECS?', 'C-DRAW2D?', 'C-RSCENE?', 'C-REPLAY?', 'C-IPC'] tool [] impl []\n== ai-assisted-authoring | expert tool | parent editor-architect | ws tools | prof ['all'] | tg ['tools'] | pl None\n  P: Evaluates and integrates AI-assisted authoring: generative asset tools, editor copilots, ML-assisted retopology/rigging/UV/LOD, provenance and licensing of generated content.\n  NR: Runtime inference ->ml-inference-runtime; License compliance sign-off ->certification-compliance\n  prov [] cons ['C-EDCMD', 'C-ASSET', 'C-ML?'] tool [] impl []\n== build-release-architect | lead process | parent engine-architect | ws release | prof ['all'] | tg [] | pl None\n  P: Build and release architecture: branching and merge model, engine release management and versioning, orchestration of the code → content → package pipeline.\n  NR: Build system implementation ->build-system-toolchains; CI pipelines ->ci-cd-automation; Packaging ->packaging-release-patching\n  prov ['C-RELEASE'] cons ['C-BUILD', 'C-PKG'] tool ['C-COOK'] impl []\n== build-system-toolchains | expert tool | parent build-release-architect | ws release | prof ['all'] | tg ['tools'] | pl None\n  P: Build graph, compiler and toolchain matrix, C++ modules/unity/PCH, compile caching and distribution, codegen integration, third-party dependencies, static analysis, build configurations.\n  NR: CI orchestration ->ci-cd-automation; Supply-chain policy ->security-engineering\n  prov ['C-BUILD'] cons [] tool [] impl []\n== ci-cd-automation | expert tool | parent build-release-architect | ws release | prof ['all'] | tg ['tools'] | pl None\n  P: CI pipelines, build farm and artifact storage, pre-submit and merge gating, symbol servers, device-farm orchestration, developer CLI and automation.\n  NR: What tests exist ->test-architect; Perf thresholds ->performance-architect\n  prov [] cons ['C-BUILD', 'C-COOK'] tool [] impl []\n== packaging-release-patching | expert tool | parent build-release-architect | ws release | prof ['all'] | tg ['tools'] | pl None\n  P: Platform packaging and signing, store-submission artifacts, delta/chunk patching, DLC, install-on-demand, client/server/content version compatibility, CDN boundary, release rollback.\n  NR: Package runtime format ->package-formats-vfs; Certification tracking ->certification-compliance\n  prov ['C-PKG'] cons ['C-VFS', 'C-BUILD', 'C-SVC', 'C-COOK', 'C-RELEASE'] tool [] impl []\n== runtime-scalability | expert runtime | parent core-runtime-architect | ws foundation | prof ['all'] | tg ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: Runtime scalability machinery: device-profile application, the registry of scalability knobs and actuators, first-run hardware auto-detect, and the closed-loop runtime governor that consumes frame-time, thermal/power and memory-pressure signals and drives registered actuators (dynamic resolution, significance, VFX, animation rate, worker count) with priorities and hysteresis.\n  NR: Budget numbers and tier definitions ->performance-architect; Hardware→tier device database ->platform-architect; Each actuator's own implementation ->owning-skill\n  prov ['C-SCALE'] cons ['C-CFG', 'C-PAL', 'C-INSTR', 'C-TASK'] tool [] impl []\n== voxel-worlds | expert runtime | parent world-architect | ws world | prof ['sandbox'] | tg ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: Chunked voxel/block worlds end to end: sparse storage and compression, meshing and remeshing on edit, runtime edit replication and persistence hand-off, block light propagation.\n  NR: Player construction gameplay (snapping, structural integrity) ->gameplay-systems-toolkit; Heightfield terrain ->terrain; Replication mechanics ->replication\n  prov [] cons ['C-WORLD', 'C-ENV', 'C-SPATIAL', 'C-RES', 'C-RSCENE?', 'C-PHYS?', 'C-REP?', 'C-SAVE?'] tool [] impl ['C-ENV']\n== gpu-platform-architect | lead runtime | parent engine-architect | ws rendering | prof ['all'] | tg ['client', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: GPU platform architecture shared by every renderer tier: layering of RHI, GPU memory, render graph, shader system, ray-query and inference infrastructure; the GPU feature-tier model (binding, pipeline-state, queue, mesh, RT, tensor tiers) and API baselines per hardware tier; task-based parallel command recording.\n  NR: Rendering pipeline and features ->render-architect; Individual API backends ->['rhi-d3d12', 'rhi-vulkan', 'rhi-metal', 'rhi-webgpu']; Frames in flight / thread existence ->frame-orchestration\n  prov ['C-GPUTIER'] cons ['C-RHI', 'C-PAL'] tool [] impl []\n== rhi-d3d12 | expert runtime | parent gpu-platform-architect | ws rendering | prof ['all'] | tg ['client', 'tools'] | pl ['pc']\n  P: Implements C-RHI on D3D12 (Agility SDK features: enhanced barriers, work graphs, SM 6.x, GPU upload heaps); owns its validation-layer runs and vendor/driver quirks.\n  NR: RHI abstraction & capability model ->rhi-core; Other API backends ->rhi-core\n  prov [] cons ['C-PAL', 'C-SYNC', 'C-GPUTIER'] tool [] impl ['C-RHI']\n== rhi-vulkan | expert runtime | parent gpu-platform-architect | ws rendering | prof ['all'] | tg ['client', 'tools'] | pl ['pc', 'mobile', 'xr-standalone']\n  P: Implements C-RHI on Vulkan (profiles incl. Android Baseline, descriptor buffers/heaps, synchronization2, dynamic rendering); owns its validation-layer runs and vendor/driver quirks.\n  NR: RHI abstraction & capability model ->rhi-core; Other API backends ->rhi-core\n  prov [] cons ['C-PAL', 'C-SYNC', 'C-GPUTIER'] tool [] impl ['C-RHI']\n== rhi-metal | expert runtime | parent gpu-platform-architect | ws rendering | prof ['all'] | tg ['client', 'tools'] | pl ['pc', 'mobile']\n  P: Implements C-RHI on Metal 3/4 (argument buffers, residency sets, MTL4 command model); owns its validation-layer runs and vendor/driver quirks.\n  NR: RHI abstraction & capability model ->rhi-core; Other API backends ->rhi-core\n  prov [] cons ['C-PAL', 'C-SYNC', 'C-GPUTIER'] tool [] impl ['C-RHI']\n== rhi-webgpu | expert runtime | parent gpu-platform-architect | ws rendering | prof ['all'] | tg ['client', 'tools'] | pl ['web']\n  P: Implements C-RHI on WebGPU (bind groups, implicit sync, limits tiers); owns its validation-layer runs and vendor/driver quirks.\n  NR: RHI abstraction & capability model ->rhi-core; Other API backends ->rhi-core\n  prov [] cons ['C-PAL', 'C-SYNC', 'C-GPUTIER'] tool [] impl ['C-RHI']\n== media-playback | expert runtime | parent render-architect | ws rendering | prof ['all'] | tg ['client', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: Pre-rendered video playback end to end: hardware/software decode backends, A/V sync against the audio clock, video surfaces for UI, world and cinematics, HDR video, package streaming.\n  NR: Movie rendering (producing video) ->cinematics-sequencer; Audio mixing ->audio-dsp-mixing\n  prov ['C-VIDEO'] cons ['C-IO', 'C-RES', 'C-GPUMEM', 'C-AUDIO', 'C-FRAME', 'C-RG'] tool [] impl []\n== vehicle-physics | expert runtime | parent physics-architect | ws simulation | prof ['vehicles'] | tg ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: Vehicle dynamics: wheeled vehicles (tires, suspension, drivetrain), aerodynamic surfaces and flight models, orbital mechanics, watercraft hydrodynamics, vehicle-specific prediction and force-feedback sources.\n  NR: Character controllers ->character-physics; Generic buoyancy ->rigid-body-dynamics; Netcode model ->prediction-rollback\n  prov [] cons ['C-PHYS', 'C-DET', 'C-ENV?', 'C-DEVICE?', 'C-PREDICT?'] tool [] impl []\n== physics-tools | expert tool | parent physics-architect | ws simulation | prof ['min2d', 'lite3d', 'std3d'] | tg ['tools'] | pl None\n  P: Physics authoring and debugging tools: collision authoring, physics-asset/ragdoll and constraint editors, the physics visual debugger/recorder, simulate-in-editor, vehicle and controller tuning, 2D collision-shape editing.\n  NR: Collision algorithms ->collision-detection; Editor host & transactions ->editor-architect\n  prov [] cons ['C-EDCMD', 'C-EDHOST', 'C-PHYS', 'C-INSTR', 'C-REPLAY?'] tool [] impl []\n== character-movement | expert runtime | parent gameplay-architect | ws gameplay | prof ['min2d', 'lite3d', 'std3d'] | tg ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: Character movement as one system at the junction of input, physics, animation and netcode: movement modes, step/slope rules, root-motion consumption and authority, networked predicted/reconciled movement with a resimulatable move API, mount/vehicle transitions, 2D platformer movement.\n  NR: Collide-and-slide controller primitive ->character-physics; Generic prediction machinery ->prediction-rollback; Animation selection ->motion-synthesis\n  prov ['C-MOVE'] cons ['C-GAME', 'C-PHYS', 'C-INPUT', 'C-ANIM?', 'C-PREDICT?', 'C-DET'] tool [] impl []\n== gameplay-data | expert runtime | parent gameplay-architect | ws gameplay | prof ['all'] | tg ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: Designer-owned data: typed data tables and row references, curve assets, tuning assets with inheritance and per-platform/difficulty variants, spreadsheet round-trip, balance simulation, and live data hotfixes through remote overrides.\n  NR: Serialization mechanics ->serialization-schema; Remote-config service ->online-services-liveops; Tabular editing widgets ->editor-ui-framework\n  prov ['C-GAMEDATA'] cons ['C-REFL', 'C-ASSET', 'C-SER', 'C-LIVE?', 'C-CFG'] tool ['C-EDCMD', 'C-EDHOST'] impl []\n== narrative-dialogue | expert runtime | parent gameplay-architect | ws gameplay | prof ['all'] | tg ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: The dialogue line model and narrative runtime shared by VO, subtitles, lip sync, localization, cinematics and AI: line database with stable IDs, branching dialogue runtime and narrative-middleware interchange, narrative fact store with save/replication participation, barks and response rules, recording scripts and placeholder VO.\n  NR: Quest content ->external:game-team; VO playback ->audio-content-runtime; String formatting ->localization-i18n\n  prov ['C-DIALOGUE'] cons ['C-LOC', 'C-SER', 'C-ID', 'C-SAVE?', 'C-REP?', 'C-A11Y'] tool ['C-EDCMD', 'C-EDHOST', 'C-GRAPH'] impl []\n== reference-games | expert process | parent program-orchestration | ws governance | prof ['all'] | tg [] | pl None\n  P: The reference-game ladder (one representative game per configuration) used as milestone and release gate, representative production-scale content sets, and the internal playtest and dogfood loop.\n  NR: Teaching samples ->developer-experience-docs; Benchmark harness ->perf-benchmarking\n  prov [] cons [] tool [] impl []\n== platform-web | expert runtime | parent platform-architect | ws platform | prof ['minimal', 'min2d', 'lite3d'] | tg ['client', 'tools'] | pl ['web']\n  P: Web target (WASM + WebGPU): threads and cross-origin isolation, memory limits, OPFS/IndexedDB storage, HTTP streaming delivery, user-gesture rules for audio/pointer/fullscreen, browser transport constraints.\n  NR: WebGPU backend ->rhi-webgpu; Browser transports ->network-transport\n  prov [] cons ['C-PAL'] tool [] impl []\n== online-services-liveops | expert runtime | parent platform-architect | ws platform | prof ['all'] | tg ['client', 'headless-client', 'server', 'tools'] | pl None\n  P: Integration boundary to third-party and own online backends and live operations: matchmaking/lobby/session boundary, remote config and feature flags, live events and experiments, service-hosted voice/text chat sessions, moderation (UGC, chat, generated content), wallet and ads boundaries, trusted time, remote generative-AI/inference boundary, service emulators and outage injection for tests.\n  NR: First-party platform services ->platform-services; Backend implementation ->external:backend; Game-server hosting ->dedicated-server\n  prov ['C-LIVE'] cons ['C-PAL', 'C-TASK', 'C-CFG', 'C-SVC?'] tool [] impl []\n== memory-performance | expert process | parent performance-architect | ws performance | prof ['all'] | tg [] | pl None\n  P: Memory as its own performance discipline: whole-process CPU+GPU+UMA footprint analysis per tier, snapshot capture and diffing, content-level attribution per asset/cell/feature, transition peak analysis, fragmentation over time; reviewer for the memory-usage obligation.\n  NR: Allocator mechanisms ->memory-allocators; Budget numbers ->performance-architect\n  prov [] cons [] tool [] impl []\n== simulation-validation | expert process | parent test-architect | ws quality | prof ['all'] | tg [] | pl None\n  P: Runs the objective validation that domain owners define for simulation-class systems: physics stability and reference suites, simulation golden traces, animation error suites, audio offline-render suites, and deterministic network simulation for prediction/replication correctness, mirroring what render-validation does for rendering.\n  NR: Defining each domain's oracles ->owning-skill; Determinism matrix definition ->determinism-replay\n  prov [] cons [] tool [] impl []\n== engine-product-management | orchestrator process | parent engine-architect | ws governance | prof ['all'] | tg [] | pl None\n  P: The engine as a product for game teams: roadmap and prioritization across game-team requirements, bug and feature intake with triage SLAs, release notes and upgrade guides, the customer-project corpus that validates each engine release, and the engine licensing model.\n  NR: Architecture decisions ->engine-architect; Work scheduling ->program-orchestration; Engine release mechanics ->build-release-architect\n  prov ['C-PROD'] cons [] tool [] impl []","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e6f72249-723b-4526-a17c-432773ec764f","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:18:38.978Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d3aa2d57-4057-40a2-af00-209484ce8006","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","vers