{"parentUuid":"116292bc-6705-496b-94f1-31bc6e9ca1c4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a14425d770a8fc220","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011djb9Veqhsds3xV7QJbvKY","type":"tool_result","content":"190:    def members(self, name):\n191-        return [s for s in self.skill_order if self.in_configuration(s, name)]\n192-\n193-    def cap_in_configuration(self, cid, name):\n194-        cap = self.cap(cid)\n195-        if cap[\"owner\"] not in self.skills or not self.in_configuration(cap[\"owner\"], name):\n196-            return False\n197-        if cap[\"profiles\"]:\n198-            profiles, _, _ = self.config(name)\n199-            return any(p in profiles for p in cap[\"profiles\"])\n200-        return True\n201-\n202-    # ---- critics\n203-    def critics_for(self, sid, stage=None):\n204-        out = []\n205-        for k, c in self.critics.items():\n206-            if stage and stage not in c[\"stages\"]:\n207-                continue\n208-            if self.scope_matches(c[\"scope\"], sid):\n209-                out.append(k)\n210-        return out\n211-\n212-    def scope_matches(self, scope, sid):\n213-        s = self.skill(sid)\n214-        for sel in scope:\n215-            if sel == \"all\":\nC-PAL 0 platform-architect  ['C-BASE'] :: Platform abstraction layer -- OS services, CPU/GPU capability discovery and device database, windowing, display & safe area, lifecycle and system events (memory pressure, thermal/power, network reachability, audio endpoint, locale, OS accessibility settings, overlay/focus, storage, page size), clocks and clock-domain correlation, processes/pipes/shared memory/dev sockets, HTTP(S)/TLS client, permissions, thread creation/affinity/QoS and main-thread dispatch. Platform code lives only in the PAL or in a registered platform backend slot.\nC-ERR 1 core-runtime-architect  ['C-BASE'] :: Error & failure model -- Result types, assertion tiers, fatal vs recoverable, degradation rules.\nC-MOD 1 core-runtime-architect  ['C-ERR', 'C-TASK'] :: Module & lifecycle -- Module descriptors, serial bootstrap then parallel init dependency graph, service registration, shutdown order, declarative self-registration (no central tables).\nC-CFG 1 core-runtime-architect  ['C-BASE'] :: Configuration & cvars -- Layered config sources (defaults, platform, device profile, remote/live, user) with precedence, typed cvars read through versioned immutable snapshots latched at sync points, queued change notification.\nC-MATH 1 math-simd-numerics  [] :: Math & numeric conventions -- Vector/matrix types, precision classes, deterministic-math variants, fixed and scalable (vector-length-agnostic) SIMD kernels, convention enforcement.\nC-MEM 1 memory-allocators  ['C-BASE'] :: Allocation & memory accounting -- Allocator interface, tagging, budgets hooks, OOM behavior.\nC-TYPES 1 containers-core-types  ['C-MEM'] :: Core types & containers -- Containers, strings, versioned stable hashing, general-purpose compression codecs, vetted cryptographic primitives wrapper, ownership/view types.\nC-SYNC 1 concurrency-primitives  ['C-BASE'] :: Concurrency primitives & thread-safety annotations -- Atomics, locks, lock-free queues, safe reclamation, thread-safety annotation conventions, OS-waitable completion tokens that IO/GPU fences plug into.\nC-TASK 1 job-system-task-graph  ['C-SYNC', 'C-MEM'] :: Task graph & job API -- Task creation, dependencies, priorities/QoS, blocking rules, completion-token integration, process-wide thread inventory with pinned/affinity lanes and middleware adapters, serial deterministic test mode and schedule-perturbation hooks, task tracing.\nC-INSTR 1 observability-telemetry  ['C-BASE'] :: Instrumentation -- Log/trace/metric API; zero cost when compiled out; trace format.\nC-CRASH 1 crash-diagnostics  ['C-BASE', 'C-INSTR'] :: Crash & diagnostic hooks -- Crash context annotations, breadcrumbs, watchdog registration.\nC-DET 1 determinism-replay  ['C-MATH'] :: Determinism -- Determinism levels, floating-point rules, ordered-execution rules, state-hash hooks.\nC-BUDGET P performance-architect  [] :: Budgets & performance gates -- Budget numbers per hardware tier × configuration × refresh class, derived from the performance model; perf gate thresholds.\nC-PLUGIN 1 plugin-system  ['C-MOD'] :: Plugin descriptor & loading -- Plugin manifest, dependency resolution, load phases, ABI tags.\nC-FRAME 2 frame-orchestration  ['C-TASK'] :: Frame, tick phases & time -- Time domains and multi-rate cadences, pipelining depth, the minimal set of named global sync points, frame-wide access declarations (ECS components and registered service resources) from which ordering is derived, the canonical simulation schedule, injectable test clock.\nC-ID 2 entity-object-model  ['C-TYPES'] :: Identity & references -- Entity IDs, GUIDs, reference kinds, lifetime rules, events.\nC-ECS 2 ecs-runtime  ['C-ID', 'C-TASK', 'C-FRAME'] :: ECS -- Components, queries, systems, access declarations, command buffers.\nC-REFL 2 reflection-metadata  ['C-TYPES'] :: Reflection & type metadata -- Type registry, properties, attributes, dynamic invocation.\nC-SER 2 serialization-schema  ['C-REFL'] :: Serialization & schema evolution -- Formats, versioning, upgraders, canonical form, untrusted-input rules.\nC-IO 2 async-io-storage  ['C-PAL', 'C-TASK'] :: Async IO -- IO requests, priorities, deadlines, completions, decompression targets.\nC-VFS 2 package-formats-vfs  ['C-IO', 'C-SER'] :: Package & VFS mounts -- Package format, mount layering (base, patch, DLC, mods, remote), chunk IDs, integrity; codec per target constrained by available hardware decompressors.\nC-ASSET 2 content-pipeline-architect  ['C-SER', 'C-ID'] :: Asset identity & references -- Asset IDs, soft/hard references, dependency declaration, registry queries.\nC-RES 2 resource-streaming-architect  ['C-ASSET', 'C-VFS', 'C-MEM'] :: Resource lifetime & streaming requests -- Resource handles and explicit lifetime; load requests with priority/deadline; the staged load pipeline (IO → decompress → fixup → GPU upload → publish) that every resource type implements; pool registration, pressure signals and shrink-by-deadline requests; residency notifications drained at a declared C-FRAME phase; fallbacks.\nC-RELOAD 2 hot-reload-iteration  ['C-RES', 'C-MOD'] :: Hot reload -- Change notifications, invalidation, state preservation hooks.\nC-SPATIAL 2 spatial-transforms  ['C-MATH', 'C-ID'] :: Transforms & spatial queries -- Transform representation incl. large-world coordinates, hierarchy, generic spatial queries, per-phase change sets (moved/attached/teleported) consumed by all spatial replicas.\nC-RHI 2 rhi-core True ['C-PAL', 'C-MEM', 'C-SYNC'] :: Render hardware interface -- Devices, queues and command recording, completion tokens, binding-model tier (bindless / descriptor-buffer / bind-group), pipeline-state-model tier (monolithic PSO / libraries / shader objects / state-object programs), GPU-generated work primitives, presentation, implicit-sync backends; the RHI consumes C-PRESENT to report present feedback.\nC-GPUMEM 2 gpu-memory-resources  ['C-RHI'] :: GPU resources & memory -- Resource creation, heaps, residency, upload/readback, lifetime.\nC-ML 2 ml-inference-runtime  ['C-TASK', 'C-MEM'] :: ML inference -- Model format and packaging, CPU and NPU backends, async invocation, precision classes, budgets.\nC-WORLD 3 world-architect  ['C-SPATIAL', 'C-RES'] :: World partition & streaming cells -- Cells, streaming sources, world data activation in budgeted, time-sliced batches with bulk registration.\nC-RG 3 render-graph-scheduling  ['C-RHI', 'C-GPUMEM'] :: Render graph -- Pass/resource declaration, queues, history resources, readback, dynamic GPU-generated work nodes; barrier output mapped or elided on implicit-sync backends.\nC-SHADER 3 shader-system  ['C-RHI'] :: Shader interface & interop -- Shader modules, permutations and budgets, binding layouts generated per binding tier, interop headers, neural/tensor intrinsics tier.\nC-MATIF 3 material-system  ['C-SHADER'] :: Material interface -- Material parameters, shading model inputs, material domains.\nC-RSCENE 3 render-architect  ['C-RG', 'C-SPATIAL', 'C-MATIF'] :: Render scene & render features -- Render features and views, render-scene data streams extracted as change-tracked deltas (no per-object proxy mirror; CPU cost O(changes)), feature registration with minimum GPU tier, non-mesh primitive kinds.\nC-TEMPORAL 3 reconstruction-upscaling  ['C-RG'] :: Temporal data -- Motion vectors, jitter, history validity, reactive/transparency masks, resolution scaling; motion-vector obligations for every moving/animated surface; UI/HUD separation for frame generation; depth+motion submission for XR spacewarp.\nC-RT 3 ray-tracing-infrastructure  ['C-RSCENE'] :: Ray queries -- Ray-query contract with hardware and software (SDF/BVH compute) backends: acceleration structures, instance data, hit/material binding, update policy.\nC-TEXT 3 text-fonts  ['C-TYPES'] :: Text layout & glyphs -- Shaped glyph runs, font fallback, glyph atlas/curve data.\nC-DRAW2D 3 render-2d-vector  ['C-RG', 'C-SHADER', 'C-TEXT'] :: 2D draw lists -- Batched 2D/vector/text draw submission used by UI, 2D games, debug overlays.\nC-PHYS 3 physics-architect  ['C-SPATIAL', 'C-FRAME', 'C-ID'] :: Physics world & scene queries -- Bodies, shapes, queries (handle-addressed, batched), contact events with budgets, stepping phases, batch add/remove O(batch), snapshot/restore/resimulate participation, collider history for rewind.\nC-ANIM 3 animation-architect  ['C-SPATIAL', 'C-ID'] :: Animation pose output -- Pose output and control input (parameters, action/montage requests, instance lifetime), root motion, animation events, pose history for rewind, network-sync hooks, physics/render hand-off.\nC-AUDIO 3 audio-architect  ['C-SPATIAL', 'C-ID'] :: Audio emitters & events -- Emitter/listener data (multiple listeners), event triggering, parameters, busses, the sample-accurate audio clock exposed to gameplay.\nC-INPUT 3 input-system  ['C-FRAME'] :: Input actions -- Action definitions and values, tick-stamped input-command frames and their serialization (all targets incl. server); device binding contexts are client-side.\nC-NET 3 network-architect  ['C-FRAME', 'C-ID'] :: Netcode model & authority policy -- Netcode model per game type, authority model, net tick and time policy, compatibility window and handshake policy.\nC-SVC 3 platform-services  ['C-PAL', 'C-TASK'] :: Platform services -- Identity tokens, entitlements & commerce, privileges, social graph, achievements, leaderboards, cloud save, region/age policy.\nC-LOC 3 localization-i18n  ['C-ASSET'] :: Localized strings -- String IDs, formatting, locale switching.\nC-UI 3 ui-architect  ['C-REFL', 'C-INPUT', 'C-DRAW2D', 'C-TEXT', 'C-LOC'] :: UI widgets & binding -- Widget model, data binding, focus, layout.\nC-NAV 3 navigation-pathfinding  ['C-SPATIAL'] :: Navigation queries -- Path requests, navmesh/grid queries, dynamic obstacles.\nC-GAME 4 gameplay-architect  ['C-ID', 'C-FRAME'] :: Gameplay framework extension -- Game module entry points, rules/session state, data-oriented control binding (input source or AI → controlled entity), scheduled gameplay systems, extension hooks.\nC-SCRIPT 3 scripting-runtime  ['C-REFL'] :: Script bindings -- Binding generation, sandbox limits, script lifecycle.\nC-SAVE 3 persistence-save  ['C-SER', 'C-ID'] :: Save games -- Save participation, versioned save records, async save/load.\nC-COOK 5 content-pipeline-architect  ['C-ASSET', 'C-SER', 'C-TASK'] :: Cook-step processors -- Processor inputs, cache keys, determinism class (bit-exact / tolerance / pinned-artifact), platform variants, world-scope steps, per-asset on-demand invocation, validation hooks.\nC-EDCMD 5 editor-architect  ['C-REFL', 'C-SER'] :: Editor commands & tool extension -- Transactions, undo/redo, selection, tool registration.\nC-GRAPH 5 graph-editor-framework  ['C-EDCMD'] :: Graph authoring & compilation -- Node/pin model, validation, compilation hooks for domain graphs.\nC-BUILD 5 build-system-toolchains  [] :: Build description -- Targets, configurations, toolchains, codegen steps.\nC-PKG 5 packaging-release-patching  ['C-VFS', 'C-BUILD'] :: Release packages & patches -- Package manifests, patch/DLC chunks, version compatibility.\nC-ARCH P engine-architect  [] :: Architecture, layering & profiles -- Layer rules, contract registry, configuration profiles, conventions.\nC-ADR P architecture-governance  [] :: ADR & fitness functions -- ADR template incl. revisit conditions; automated architectural checks.\nC-EVID P research-evidence  [] :: Evidence grading -- Source tiers, maturity classes, claim standards.\nC-ORCH P program-orchestration  [] :: Agent coordination protocol -- Ownership ledger with access classes; write sets by module convention (src/<skill-id>/, tools/<skill-id>/; tests owned by the test-owning skill); shared-file protocol; contributor semantics (review + change request, never direct writes); change requests; integration order and milestones; human-gate tasks; failure triage; per-change provenance; critic gates with calibration and independent adjudication.\nC-TEST P test-architect  [] :: Test & validation definition of done -- Required test kinds per skill, test determinism, coverage & mutation thresholds, the evidence bundle an implementer hands to S3/S4 critics, oracle independence, conformance suites owned by contract owners with consumer-driven additions.\nC-API P api-lifecycle-migration  [] :: API stability & deprecation -- Public vs internal APIs, versioning, deprecation windows, upgraders.\nC-TRUST P security-engineering  [] :: Trust boundaries -- Untrusted inputs list, validation obligations, sandbox rules.\nC-A11Y P accessibility  [] :: Accessibility requirements -- Mapped guideline requirements per player-facing feature.\nC-BASE 0 platform-architect  [] :: Bootstrap base -- Raw page allocator, raw log/assert/abort sink, monotonic clock, raw thread primitives and late-bound hook tables that higher layers install (allocator, log sink, assert handler, crash annotator). Depends on nothing.\nC-LIFETIME 1 core-runtime-architect  ['C-SYNC'] :: Ownership & retirement -- Engine-wide ownership and cross-thread reference rules; deferred-destruction/retirement service keyed to completion tokens (task completion, frames in flight, GPU fences).\nC-IPC 2 core-runtime-architect  ['C-PAL', 'C-TASK'] :: Engine IPC -- Process model and IPC/RPC transport for editor↔runtime, tool workers, crash handler, profiler and script debugger; dev-only port security.\nC-SCALE 1 runtime-scalability  ['C-CFG'] :: Scalability & governor -- Device-profile knobs, scalability cvars, budget query/report API, actuator registration and governor control signals.\nC-FLOW 2 frame-orchestration  ['C-FRAME'] :: Cross-subsystem data channels -- Versioned snapshots, double/triple-buffered hand-off, mailboxes and multi-rate resampling between subsystems; producer/consumer declared per channel. The default for runtime data flow; global barriers need an ADR.\nC-PRESENT 2 frame-orchestration  ['C-FRAME'] :: Present timeline -- Present timeline and display-time prediction, latency markers, interposed presenters (frame generation, XR compositor, cloud encoder), GPU-frame-complete and present-feedback sink implemented by the RHI (dependency inversion).\nC-SNAPSHOT 2 determinism-replay  ['C-FRAME', 'C-SER'] :: Frame-state snapshot & resimulation -- Snapshot/restore, resimulate N ticks, history ring, per-participant cost declaration.\nC-REPLAY 3 determinism-replay  ['C-SNAPSHOT', 'C-SER'] :: Replay container & streams -- Replay container, timeline, stream registration (input, replication, visual log, animation debug, external/nondeterministic inputs) and cross-build versioning.\nC-VIEW 2 spatial-transforms  ['C-SPATIAL'] :: Views & view arbitration -- View registry: view sources (gameplay camera, cinematic, editor, photo mode, XR pose) with priority/blend stack and shake/FOV channels, per-local-player views, view origin for LWC rebasing; derived listener and streaming-source signals for sinks.\nC-SIGNIF 2 world-architect  ['C-VIEW'] :: Significance & simulation tiers -- Per-entity significance, simulation tier and update budget, computed once from views/players (all players on a server) and consumed by each domain's LOD policy.\nC-ENV 3 world-architect  ['C-SPATIAL'] :: Environment queries -- Environment query service: ground height/surface type, water surface/volume (height, velocity, depth, body id), wind field, weather parameters, deformation deltas; implemented by terrain, water, atmosphere and voxel providers; headless-capable.\nC-GPUTIER 2 gpu-platform-architect  ['C-RHI'] :: GPU feature tiers -- Named GPU feature tiers (binding model, pipeline-state model, queue topology, mesh/RT/tensor support, memory model) and the API baseline each tier maps to; render features declare the minimum tier they need.\nC-INSTANCES 3 geometry-pipeline  ['C-RG', 'C-GPUMEM'] :: Instance scene -- Persistent instance/primitive handles, batched add/remove/update with delta upload (cost O(changes)), instance data layout shared with the ray-tracing instance builder; served by both CPU and GPU submission paths.\nC-GEOLOD 3 virtualized-geometry-lod  ['C-RG'] :: Geometry LOD & page residency -- Cluster/LOD selection and page residency for raster, shadow and ray-tracing consumers.\nC-VT 3 texture-streaming-vt  ['C-RG', 'C-GPUMEM'] :: Texture residency & virtual texturing -- Texture residency requests, VT page tables/feedback and allocation for terrain, materials and runtime-composited textures.\nC-LIGHT 3 direct-lighting-shadows  ['C-RSCENE'] :: Direct lighting sampling -- Light lists (clustered or stochastic), shadow lookups, light units, many-light sampling API for any shading point incl. translucency, volumes and particles.\nC-GI 3 global-illumination  ['C-RSCENE'] :: Indirect lighting sampling -- Indirect diffuse/specular sampling for any shading point (incl. translucent and volumetric), probes, sky/environment lighting.\nC-ATMOS 3 atmosphere-weather  ['C-RSCENE'] :: Atmosphere & participating media -- Aerial perspective, froxel/local media volumes, cloud shadows, weather-driven global material parameters.\nC-VIDEO 3 media-playback  ['C-RG'] :: Video surfaces -- Video playback sessions, surfaces as textures, timing against the audio clock.\nC-DEVICE 2 input-devices-haptics  ['C-PAL'] :: Input devices & haptics -- Device enumeration, raw state and events with timestamps, device↔platform-user pairing, haptic, trigger-effect and LED output, virtual device injection for automation.\nC-NETLINK 2 network-transport  ['C-PAL', 'C-TASK'] :: Network links & sessions -- Sessions, channels, reliability/ordering classes, send budgets, link statistics, connection events; used by replication, voice, rollback input exchange and telemetry streams.\nC-REP 3 replication  ['C-NETLINK', 'C-SER', 'C-ID'] :: Replication -- Replicated state declaration, relevancy hooks, RPCs, net IDs, batch registration, replay and spectator streams.\nC-PREDICT 3 prediction-rollback  ['C-REP', 'C-DET', 'C-SNAPSHOT', 'C-INPUT'] :: Prediction & rollback -- Predicted/rollback-able state registration, tick-stamped input history, resimulation hooks, rewind queries, cosmetic-effect suppression during resim.\nC-MOVE 4 character-movement  ['C-PHYS', 'C-GAME'] :: Character movement -- Movement modes, move requests, resimulatable move API, root-motion hand-off.\nC-GAMEDATA 3 gameplay-data  ['C-REFL', 'C-ASSET'] :: Gameplay data -- Data tables, curve assets, tuning assets with overrides, live override layer.\nC-DIALOGUE 3 narrative-dialogue  ['C-LOC', 'C-ID'] :: Dialogue lines & narrative state -- Line records (speaker, text per locale, VO per locale, timing, lip-sync data), conditions, playback requests, narrative fact store.\nC-AIAGENT 4 ai-behavior-perception  ['C-GAME'] :: AI decision-provider extension point -- Optional decision providers (learned policies, LLM agents) with budget, timeout, moderation and authored fallback.\nC-A11YRT 3 accessibility  ['C-TEXT'] :: Accessibility runtime -- Caption/subtitle submission, screen-reader announcements and accessibility-tree ingestion, TTS/STT, accessibility settings and change events.\nC-DEVUI 3 visual-debugging-tools  ['C-DRAW2D'] :: Developer UI -- Immediate-mode developer UI and debug menus available in development builds on every target.\nC-EDHOST 5 editor-ui-framework  ['C-EDCMD'] :: Editor host -- Asset-editor host, preview-scene registration, thumbnail providers, inspector customization, tool-mode registration, shared curve/timeline widgets.\nC-LIVE 3 online-services-liveops  ['C-PAL', 'C-TASK'] :: Online & live-ops services -- Sessions/matchmaking tickets, remote config, events/experiments, chat sessions, moderation, generative/inference service calls with quotas, trusted time, service emulation.\nC-XRVIEW 3 xr-runtime  ['C-VIEW'] :: XR views -- View poses, projections, foveation maps, compositor layers and spacewarp depth/motion submission.\nC-MLGPU 3 ml-inference-runtime  ['C-RG', 'C-ML'] :: GPU inference -- Inference as a render-graph pass under async-compute and budget scheduling; weights for in-shader networks.\nC-CERT P certification-compliance  [] :: External requirements register -- Register of external requirements per program (console cert, Steam Deck Verified, store review, law) each mapped to an owning capability; owners must satisfy their entries.\nC-PERF P performance-architect  [] :: Performance findings protocol -- Finding format (hypothesis, capture, attribution, expected gain), routing as a change request to the owning skill, time-boxed territory loans recorded in the ledger.\nC-BENCH P perf-benchmarking  [] :: Benchmark registration -- Benchmark registration, metric schema, C-BUDGET line reference, warm-up and variance rules, required hardware tier, replay-driven runs.\nC-PROD P engine-product-management  [] :: Engine roadmap & intake -- Roadmap priorities consumed by work decomposition, intake/triage SLAs, release-note obligations.\nC-RELEASE P build-release-architect  [] :: Release model -- Branch model, release trains, version identifiers, client/server/content compatibility keys, LTS and hotfix streams.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"243b9b6e-f671-42b1-906c-8eef6af03b61","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:19:07.581Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"116292bc-6705-496b-94f1-31bc6e9ca1c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
