{"parentUuid":"c5bc9262-558a-45a6-aad6-94b256e8f533","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a14425d770a8fc220","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hxa64SvzkbF5SJwFQpmPEP","type":"tool_result","content":"[('ARCH', 44), ('PLAT', 85), ('CORE', 107), ('RES', 23), ('CNT', 39), ('WLD', 59), ('RND', 191), ('ML', 6), ('PHY', 63), ('ANM', 50), ('AUD', 31), ('INP', 23), ('NET', 54), ('GAM', 81), ('UI', 39), ('ED', 51), ('BLD', 35), ('QA', 53), ('PRF', 36), ('OBS', 20), ('XC', 55)]\n# ARCH Engine architecture, governance & agent organization\n ## ARCH.REQ\n   game-requirements | Capture target game requirements (genre, scale, platforms, online model) as engine requirements | engine-architect E |  \n   profiles | Engine configuration profiles & feature sets (indie 2D → AAA open-world online) | engine-architect E |  \n   hardware-tiers | Hardware tier definitions incl. server instance classes and refresh-rate classes | engine-architect E | performance-architect,dedicated-server \n   non-goals | Capability & non-goal register (radar non-goals) | engine-architect E |  \n   platform-matrix | Supported-target matrix (OS × ISA × GPU API × store × support tier) | engine-architect E | platform-architect,build-system-toolchains,ci-cd-automation,certification-compliance \n ## ARCH.STRUCT\n   layering | Layering rules & module boundaries | engine-architect E |  \n   contracts | Contract registry between subsystems | engine-architect E |  \n   build-buy | Build / integrate / buy decisions (middleware, OSS) | engine-architect E | architecture-governance \n   replaceability | Subsystem replaceability & optionality (modules absent in small profiles) | engine-architect E |  \n   conventions | Global conventions: units, handedness, up-axis, coordinate spaces | engine-architect E | math-simd-numerics \n   arbitration | Cross-domain arbitration & escalation of boundary disputes | engine-architect E |  \n   platform-backends | Registered platform backend slots (RHI, IO, audio endpoint, input, sockets, crash, save storage, service SDK, IME/a11y bridge) | platform-architect E | architecture-governance \n   registration | Declarative self-registration for phases, render features, services, cvars, codegen inputs (no central tables) | engine-architect E | frame-orchestration,render-architect \n   binding | Contract binding policy: implementation chosen at compile/link/load time; batch-granular interfaces; no per-item virtual dispatch across contracts on hot paths | engine-architect E | cpu-performance,architecture-governance \n ## ARCH.GOV\n   adr | ADR lifecycle with evidence, alternatives, revisit conditions | architecture-governance E |  \n   fitness | Automated architectural fitness functions (layering, dependency, contract conformance) | architecture-governance E |  \n   anti-legacy | Anti-legacy review against the flagged-pattern catalogue (data/legacy-patterns.json) | architecture-governance E |  \n   radar | Technology radar (data/radar.json): maturity, owners, revisit triggers, non-goals | architecture-governance E | research-evidence \n   process-tiers | Governance weight per organization tier (which ADR/CR/critic stages are mandatory) | architecture-governance E |  \n ## ARCH.EVID\n   grading | Source grading & provenance tiers | research-evidence E |  \n   survey | Literature survey protocol per decision | research-evidence E |  \n   spike | Prototype/spike protocol producing evidence where literature is thin | research-evidence E |  \n   claims | Benchmark-backed claims standard | research-evidence E | perf-benchmarking \n ## ARCH.ORG\n   decomposition | Milestone → task decomposition by skill territory | program-orchestration E |  \n   ownership-ledger | Ownership ledger & territory locks | program-orchestration E |  \n   integration | Integration sequencing & milestone vertical slices | program-orchestration E |  \n   change-requests | Contract change-request protocol between agents | program-orchestration E | architecture-governance \n   critic-gates | Scheduling critic gates per stage | program-orchestration E |  \n   bootstrap | Walking-skeleton definition & bring-up order | program-orchestration E | engine-architect,platform-architect,ci-cd-automation \n   milestones | Milestone ladder with per-milestone skill set, contract maturity & exit criteria (data/milestones.json) | program-orchestration E | reference-games \n   write-sets | Module/file write-set convention & shared-file protocol | program-orchestration E | build-system-toolchains \n   staffing | Agent staffing tiers: co-hosting of skills per organization scale (by workstream) | program-orchestration E |  \n   escalation | Escalation tiers & decision SLAs; delegated arbitration inside a lead's subtree | program-orchestration E | engine-architect \n   human-gates | Register of decisions requiring human authorization (contracts, spend, NDA access, submissions, legal sign-off) | program-orchestration E | engine-architect,certification-compliance \n   risk | Program risk register & risk-driven milestone ordering | program-orchestration E | research-evidence \n   triage | Failure attribution, bisection, routing to owners, revert-first policy | program-orchestration E | ci-cd-automation,perf-benchmarking \n   critic-calibration | Critic calibration via seeded defects; rounds count only above recall threshold | program-orchestration E | test-architect \n   adjudication | Independent adjudication of rejected and partially accepted findings | program-orchestration E |  \n   provenance | Per-change agent/model/task attestation in the ledger | program-orchestration E | security-engineering \n ## ARCH.PROD\n   roadmap | Roadmap & prioritization across game-team requirements | engine-product-management E |  \n   intake | Game-team bug & feature intake and triage SLAs | engine-product-management E |  \n   release-notes | Release notes, changelogs & upgrade guides | engine-product-management E | developer-experience-docs \n   customer-corpus | Customer/reference project corpus validating each release | engine-product-management E | api-lifecycle-migration,functional-automation-soak \n   licensing-model | Engine licensing & terms model for game teams | engine-product-management E |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a7be8717-5757-4204-a4c2-e05b6000fa75","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:21:38.040Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c5bc9262-558a-45a6-aad6-94b256e8f533","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
